              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "জুতো (juto) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from yukta, \"joined, yoked\" (CDIAL 10479). CDIAL lists Bengali jutā, \"shoe\", under it."
